00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.133
Why do we do this so far from the fridge?

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:32.963
This is like the opposite
of track and field.

00:11:33.837 --> 00:11:36.200
Woo! (laughs)

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:38.950
That was honestly the hardest
part of this whole thing.

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:41.450
Actually, no it wasn't. (laughs)

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:42.503
Is this day five?

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:43.920
- [Crew Member] This is day five.

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:46.210
- Hmm, how did we get here? (laughs)

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:49.920
So, I've let my rain drop
cake chill overnight,

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:54.140
but before I even flip it,
which I am terrified to do,

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:56.663
I'm gonna make my brown sugar syrup.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:12:00.260
So all it takes is two cups of brown sugar

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:02.363
and one cup of water.

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:04.963
We're doing a lot of
dissolving in this process.

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:06.560
All it is is dissolving.

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:10.390
Now I'm just gonna let it cool
down and it will thicken up

00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:12.513
which is the beauty of a syrup.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:16.780
Okay, we've made it, it is
time to flip this thing.

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:21.780
I am really, really, really,
really, really, really,

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:24.563
really nervous.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:27.700
I should've gone to pee before this.

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:29.587
It literally looks like water in here.

00:12:29.587 --> 00:12:31.303
Just, you know, go for it.

00:12:33.761 --> 00:12:35.700
God, get my hand out of there, (beep)

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:39.450
(triumphant classical music)

00:12:40.648 --> 00:12:42.731
(laughs)

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:44.263
Oh my God, I did it!

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:46.103
Okay, here we go.

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:47.083
Woo.

00:12:47.083 --> 00:12:48.130
Oh my God, I'm shaking, okay.

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:49.693
We've got some rain.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:52.820
I'm gonna put this soybean
flour around the edge.

00:12:52.820 --> 00:12:54.570
Looks super good, it's like rustic.

00:12:56.112 --> 00:12:57.600
I did it!

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:00.940
♪ I did it, I did it, I did ♪

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:03.580
I have to say the toppings
really do make this.

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:05.900
You get the sweetness
from the syrup we made

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:07.990
and then the roasted soybean flour

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:09.860
kind of gives it a nuttiness,

00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:14.053
and it's also super refreshing
so a great summer dessert.

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:18.721
Wet. (Alex and crew member laugh)

00:13:18.721 --> 00:13:21.554
(classical music)

00:13:32.923 --> 00:13:35.756
(camera shutters)

